# Uncorrelated subqueries as values in a query block that does not aggregate (ADR 0041's SQ2, its first PR): a
# select item -- alone, in arithmetic, functions, COALESCE, casts and CASE (EXISTS in its WHEN) -- an ORDER BY item and
# a SELECT DISTINCT's list, through the value's single row, joined before any row is read; and the select lists of
# EXISTS (dropped, as DuckDB drops it), IN, scalar, derived-table, CTE and set-operation blocks.

# ---- SQ2a: select items and DISTINCT of a block that does not aggregate ----

# A value as a select item of a block that does not aggregate: computed once, before any row is read, and the same
# on every row. Its type is the subquery's column: one row's value, NULL over no row or a NULL row, VARCHAR, DECIMAL,
