# A value of two rows fails, in both engines, even where no row reads it: its join is built before any row is read,
# so over an empty table, a WHERE (or an IN of an empty subquery, or an outer join's WHERE) that keeps no row, an
# untaken CASE branch, a COALESCE whose first argument is never NULL, a value multiplied by zero, LIMIT 1, DISTINCT,
# and a UNION ALL of two one-row arms.

